# SELinux domains of the service bundles that do not run in the default one
# (untrusted_service_bundle). Read at boot by the SDV lifecycle manager
# (system/software_defined_vehicle/lifecycle_management, agent.rs and selinux_policy_reader.rs):
#   <APEX package>.<BundleName>   <full SELinux context>
# The package is the bundle's APEX (com.everyware.wifi), not the catalog's (com.everyware), and
# the context goes to setexeccon() as written. A line that does not match leaves the bundle in
# the default domain without an error.
# The Wi-Fi bundle talks to wpa_supplicant's control interface, which no other bundle may
# (device/rb3/sdv_media_db845c/sepolicy, bundles/wifi/README.md).
com.everyware.wifi.WifiServiceBundle u:r:wifi_service_bundle:s0
# The Matter bundle speaks Matter on the house's network: UDP and mDNS multicast, which the
# default domain has not (device/rb3/sdv_media_db845c/sepolicy, bundles/matter/README.md).
com.everyware.matter.MatterServiceBundle u:r:matter_service_bundle:s0
# The System bundle sets the time zone (persist.sys.timezone), which no other bundle may
# (device/rb3/sdv_media_db845c/sepolicy, bundles/system/README.md).
com.everyware.system.SystemServiceBundle u:r:system_service_bundle:s0
